sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: the task VM role phases (software, tools, check), the same Ansible phases that build the task image (docs/cli/tasks/vm-image-build.mmd), applied to a running task VM. Stage 2 of the command development pipeline runs it once when a change holds playbooks or pins; stage 6 runs it on the refresh VM.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · task-vms:converge on the Gateway host
  %% kind: task_vm.converge
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant VM as Task VM<br/>running
  Note over GW: Admit the converge<br/>task-vms:converge VM
  %%> When:
  %%> - `php artisan task-vms:converge VM [--nfs-checkout=PATH --nfs-subnet=CIDR --nfs-interface=nested]`
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the task VM is `ready` and its guest Node is active with a recorded SSH host key
  %%> - no other Operation holds the VM (`operation.target_busy`)
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - the recipe.json of the release, the Vite+ lock, the VM's SSH target with its host key, and the Pi server digest with its place on the Gateway host
  %%> - the NFS settings when named: the checkout to export, the nested subnet and the nested bridge
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-vm-converge
  SW->>SW: Write the intent<br/>private run folder
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the intent to a private file and locates the shipped playbooks
  SW->>GW: Fetch the Pi server<br/>copy over ssh
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - copies the Pi server from the Gateway host to the run folder on 209
  %%> Why:
  %%> - Pi is an internal artifact, not a download; the playbook copies it on to the VM only when the VM's copy differs from the pin
  SW->>SW: Check the Pi server<br/>sha256 of the pin
  SW->>SW: Write the playbook input<br/>inventory · vars · hosts
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - writes the inventory, the variables and `known_hosts` from the intent; the VM's host key is the recorded one
  SW->>VM: Install the software<br/>Ansible phase: software
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - apt packages at the pins of the recipe, from the Ubuntu snapshot through their own apt configuration
  %%> - Node, pnpm, Bun and Vite+, Rust, the Swamp binary and the Pi server
  %%> - a tool that already shows its pinned version is left alone, so a VM at the pins reports no change
  SW->>VM: Install the tools<br/>Ansible phase: tools
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the NFS server; with NFS settings it exports the checkout to the nested subnet only (`rw,async`) and allows port 2049 from the nested bridge in UFW
  %%> - the shape gate linters in `/opt/orbit-shape-gate`, named by the digest of their pins, so the handoff check runs offline
  SW->>VM: Check the task VM role<br/>Ansible phase: check
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the one end check: every package at its pin, every runtime and tool at its version, the NFS server active, the exports as named
  alt the check passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and the end check's status; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the converge<br/>recipe identity
  else a phase fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    %%> On the VM:
    %%> - finished phases stay; there is no rollback. Run the same command again: each phase skips what matches
  end
  SW->>SW: Remove the playbook input<br/>always
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the intent and the Pi copy do not outlive the run, whatever its result
